-- EXPECT-ERROR: which has side effects
-- Capabilities widening, Task 5 (F2 fix) -- `cap pure` (`check_pure_module`,
-- `typecheck.ml:6581`), the REJECT side for the RNG source: a `cap pure`
-- module whose body calls the REAL effectful builtin `random_bytes`
-- (`builtin_cap_table` maps it to `IO.Random`, `typecheck.ml:1064`). Pre-fix,
-- `pure_banned` spelled `random_int`/`random_float`/`random_bool` (names that
-- DO NOT EXIST as builtins) and MISSED the real `random_bytes` -- so this
-- program typechecked with exit 0 (UNSOUND). The F2 fix derives `pure_banned`
-- from `builtin_cap_table`, so `random_bytes` is now banned. `random_bytes :
-- Int -> Bytes` is total, so `: Bytes` is a correct signature and the ONLY
-- rejection is `check_pure_module`'s own: `` `gen` in `mod LeakyPure`
-- (declared `cap pure`) calls `random_bytes`, which has side effects. `` (A
-- WARNING-level Check 1b body-scan diagnostic -- "requires `Cap(IO.Random)`"
-- -- also fires alongside, per F1; it does not change the exit code and is
-- not the substring pinned here.) See core-march-types.md §2.8.11.
mod LeakyPure do
  needs IO.Random
  cap pure

  fn gen() : Bytes do
    random_bytes(16)
  end
end
